# Implementation Plan: MediSense RAG Generation Pipeline

Build a provider-agnostic, structured RAG Generation Pipeline in `com.medisense.rag.generation` featuring system prompt enforcement, structured context assembly, dual LLM provider support (Gemini + local Ollama fallback), circuit breaker resilience, and robust JSON parsing.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Generation Architecture**:
> - **PromptAssembler**: Builds system instruction, retrieved context tags (`[Context N - Source: X Y]`), patient structured lab/prescription data, user query, and language instructions (Tamil non-translation notes for drug/numeric fields).
> - **System Prompt**: Hardcoded, version-controlled string enforcing: (1) Answer ONLY from context, (2) return `INSUFFICIENT_CONTEXT` when unanswerable, (3) no prescriptions/diagnoses, (4) no dosage/interaction mentions, (5) `[Source: X]` tags, (6) JSON output schema.
> - **LLM Providers & Resiliency**:
>   - `GeminiProvider`: Primary provider (Temperature 0.1, 1000 max tokens, 10s timeout).
>   - `OllamaProvider`: Secondary fallback provider (`mistral:7b-instruct-q4_K_M`, Temperature 0.1, 30s timeout).
>   - `GeminiCircuitBreaker`: 3 failures in 60s -> opens circuit for 5 minutes (300,000 ms), bypassing Gemini to Ollama.
> - **ResponseParser**: Markdown fence stripping (````json ... ````), `INSUFFICIENT_CONTEXT` handling, JSON validation, and parse failure fallbacks.
> - **GenerationOrchestrator**: Coordinates Assembly -> Execution -> Parsing -> Delivery.

